    "title": "Spurs vs. Grizzlies: How to watch the game, who's starting, who's out",
    "text": "Spurs (54-18) vs. Grizzlies (24-47) When/where: 7 p.m. Wednesday at FedEx Forum, Memphis, Tenn. TV/radio: FanDuel Sports SW; 1200 AM, 1350 AM (Spanish), 107.5 FM (Spanish). PROBABLE STARTERSSpurs: PG De'Aaron Fox (6-3, 9th year), SG Stephon Castle (6-6, 2nd); SF Devin Vassell (6-5, 6th), PF Julian Champagnie (6-7, 4th), C Victor Wembanyama (7-4, 3rd).  Grizzlies: PG Walter Clayton Jr. (6-3, 1st), SG Javon Small (6-1, 1st), SF Jaylen Wells (6-6, 2nd), PF G.G. Jackson II (6-9, 3rd), C Olivier-Maxence Prosper (6-8, 3rd). RESERVESSpurs: G/F Keldon Johnson (6-6, 7th), G Dylan Harper (6-6, 1st), C Luke Kornet (7-1, 9th), F Harrison Barnes (6-7, 14th), C Bismack Biyombo (6-8, 15th), G Lindy Waters III (6-5, 5th), C/F Kelly Olynyk (6-11, 13th) G Jordan McLaughlin (5-11, 7th) F Carter Bryant (6-6, 1st), C Mason Plumlee (7-0, 13th). Inactive: David Jones Garcia (two-way), Harrison Ingram (two-way), Emanuel Miller (two-way). Grizzlies: F Tyler Burton (6-7, 1st), F/C Taj Gibson (6-9, 17th), F Taylor Hendricks (6-9, 3rd), G Dejon Jarreau (6-5, 2nd), G Ty Jerome (6-5, 7th), G Cam Spencer  (6-3, 2nd). Inactive: Ja Morant (left elbow sprain), Scotty Pippen Jr. (right big toe surgery), Jahmai Mashack (left ankle sprain), Zach Edey (left ankle surgery), Cedric Coward (personal reasons), Brandon Clarke (right calf strain), Kentavious Caldwell-Pope (right hand surgery), Santi Aldama (right knee surgery), Rayan Rupert (G League). COACHESSpurs: Mitch Johnson.Grizzlies: Tuomas Iisalo. STAT LEADERSSpurs: Points, Wembanyama (24.3 per game). Rebounds, Wembanyama (11.1). Assists, Castle (7.1). Steals, Castle/Fox (1.2). Blocks, Wembanyama (3.0). Grizzlies: Points, Jerome (19.9 per game). Rebounds, Edey (11.1). Assists, Morant (8.1), Steals, Pippen (1.9), Blocks, Edey (1.9). NOTABLE• With a victory Wednesday, the Spurs can clinch home-court advantage in the first round of the playoffs. A win combined with a L.A. Lakers loss at Indiana would secure the No. 2 seed in the Western Conference for the Spurs. • The Spurs are 16-2 this season with their most-used starting lineup intact (Fox, Castle, Vassell, Champagnie, Wembanyama). The injury-depleted Grizzlies have employed 36 different starting lineups, with only one of them used more than eight times. • In his third season, Wembanyama has reached 4,000 career points and 600 blocks. Since the NBA began tracking blocked shots in 1975-76, the only other player to hit those marks in his first 175 games was former Spurs great David Robinson.  Jeff McDonald",
